  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 402.55 Sacrificial anode system",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 402.55 “Sacrificial anode system” means a type of cathodic protection system that uses zinc or magnesium anodes buried in the ground close to the metal surface that are connected to the surface being protected by a wire.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Or 400) #10393, eff 9-1-13; ss by #12643, eff 10-10-18 (formerly Env-Or 402.45) (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Or 400)",
